<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil drops, buyers step back.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil drops, buyers step back.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.7255)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     33.10/33.30     19.18/19.30   33.30/33.50</p>
<p> BREMEN		33.10/33.30     19.18/19.30   33.30/33.50</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    33.00/33.20     19.12/19.24   33.10/33.30</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   33.50/33.80     19.41/19.59   33.70/34.00</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   33.60/33.90     19.47/19.65   33.80/34.10</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  34.70/35.00     20.11/20.28   34.80/35.20</p>
<p>German inland gas oil dropped on Thursday as gas oil futures came off. Buying interest, which has been good, was slowed. &quot;People see weaker prices and they hold out in the hope of even lower prices the next day,&quot; commented one trader.</p>
</text>
